[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83618"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ as shown in the table below, compute $a+b+c.$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $a$ | $0.5$ | $b$ | $c$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =F(1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =F(3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4 \\\\  & =0.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $c,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =F(4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4+0.1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.3+0.9+1=2.2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-1/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" :answer/id #uuid "c276bdf5-a110-53c4-ae6d-41e106956fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "2d02ab43-6b13-513a-b121-32f657ea8a5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf074358-f873-5439-b81e-2bd426f9199e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275826/field-1/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-275826/field-1/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" "q-275826/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-2/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "808d2ee5-c157-5267-ac77-4e722eef8a94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "419202f6-6ce9-5e9e-9da7-409a52a2f07f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275826/field-2/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer-field/choices ["q-275826/field-2/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-3/64dac4e8f093be5366d519b3629f169a9ad0c7dcff60d55c0c5d41febb3ce748" :answer/id #uuid "392ac5d9-80a7-5d9a-8a18-74fb9b2ea678" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.85" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8654f89-5f82-55b2-b9f2-7708f8c814df" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275826/field-3/64dac4e8f093be5366d519b3629f169a9ad0c7dcff60d55c0c5d41febb3ce748" :answer-field/choices ["q-275826/field-3/64dac4e8f093be5366d519b3629f169a9ad0c7dcff60d55c0c5d41febb3ce748"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275826" :question/id #uuid "c337a22c-9b10-530f-9e90-224636a7ab2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275826" :question/problem "For a discrete random variable $Y,$ the probability mass function $f(y)$ and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ are shown in the table below. Fill in the blanks.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.10$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.20$ | $0.15$ |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.10$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $F(2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25+0.30 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(4),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25+0.30+0.20 \\\\  & =0.85.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275826/field-1" "q-275826/field-2" "q-275826/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9ea7a5-3ec2-516c-a755-bc9c7346efeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275826"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275824/field-1/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe" :answer/id #uuid "7bfa3dcc-1acf-598e-8a43-c375faf977db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275824/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "08d262d5-165c-56da-b896-957c38378b40" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275824/field-1/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-275824/field-1/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275824" :question/id #uuid "2b442ef7-d587-5dd6-aff9-0403f1e56cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-275824" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ (as shown in the table below) and the cumulative distribution function $F(y),$ compute $F(2).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.10$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ | $0.40$ |\n\n$F(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.10+0.05+0.45 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275824/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9ea7a5-3ec2-516c-a755-bc9c7346efeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335957/field-1/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" :answer/id #uuid "afe49d7f-6c91-505b-8f18-88956d8dd97b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335957/field-1/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" :answer/id #uuid "43606f9b-3692-5e25-a711-960874b893c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335957/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "909f417e-0e4e-56fa-baa8-1a84adf31de4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335957/field-1/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-335957/field-1/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" "q-335957/field-1/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335957" :question/id #uuid "de5c2841-ae71-54e5-934e-b83205683209" :question/math-academy-id "q-335957" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ (as shown in the table below) and the cumulative distribution function $F(y),$ compute $F(3).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ |\n\n$F(3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.20+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335957/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9ea7a5-3ec2-516c-a755-bc9c7346efeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335957"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335964/field-1/89ea20d0211adec86f2cf7addcc2251cde829a7f1f7bab8924e6f7898bb20876" :answer/id #uuid "6fd01f1b-6f25-563a-954b-3e658d5bdce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.189" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335964/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c9a4cef-b6ec-55c7-801a-d0dba4bb3cec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335964/field-1/89ea20d0211adec86f2cf7addcc2251cde829a7f1f7bab8924e6f7898bb20876" :answer-field/choices ["q-335964/field-1/89ea20d0211adec86f2cf7addcc2251cde829a7f1f7bab8924e6f7898bb20876"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335964" :question/id #uuid "a3ecabfa-6d6f-5467-9153-7528fa70c11b" :question/math-academy-id "q-335964" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ (as shown in the table below) and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$, compute $F(2)-F(1).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.343$ | $0.441$ | $0.189$ | $0.027$ |\n\n$F(2)-F(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $F(1)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(Y\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =0.343+0.441 \\\\  & =0.784.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(2)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.343+0.441+0.189 \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nF(2)-F(1)=0.973-0.784=0.189\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335964/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9ea7a5-3ec2-516c-a755-bc9c7346efeb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335964"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "aac8a01d-9749-5d1d-bfc2-a0bc9fa776ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "6912bf03-e341-5ac5-939f-ac82cc1cfa1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "b76f23d6-46eb-54e5-a1a8-07f2f8735459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "5d7236d5-893c-5d51-ba3f-35152439d1f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902/selection/7ca406ed6690410e3c85c046a8fc266540a56cf4545cf1cbb6354f4fdf108590" :answer/id #uuid "e187bd84-e0a9-5c32-8c4f-35604f217a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91e26cba-a029-5212-88b7-096629c1d49c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83902/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer-field/choices ["q-83902/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-83902/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-83902/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-83902/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-83902/selection/7ca406ed6690410e3c85c046a8fc266540a56cf4545cf1cbb6354f4fdf108590"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83902" :question/id #uuid "afc8a59c-e258-5eb9-9921-f520a5bbd71d" :question/math-academy-id "q-83902" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=6).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,2,4,6}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=2)+P(X=4)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,2,4})+P(X=6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83902/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2bc3af7-207d-5f4f-9d8c-94f441ef1686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335999/field-1/09f9568b9032a258744b73b08553a45679ce3baf10e1847349ddb9cf78a3d261" :answer/id #uuid "9a9c7121-a23b-5866-96d4-068636f119da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335999/field-1/0064d374f806cba8ea43a11831d2980495c6733de7e909ec06431bd236f4f2b3" :answer/id #uuid "5a74989b-e600-567c-8c96-36a2ae41f01b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335999/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bca9cf8-7fb6-5454-ab7c-5718135f6cc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335999/field-1/09f9568b9032a258744b73b08553a45679ce3baf10e1847349ddb9cf78a3d261" :answer-field/choices ["q-335999/field-1/09f9568b9032a258744b73b08553a45679ce3baf10e1847349ddb9cf78a3d261" "q-335999/field-1/0064d374f806cba8ea43a11831d2980495c6733de7e909ec06431bd236f4f2b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335999" :question/id #uuid "9837fbcb-d318-5d2d-b11a-6e33be305094" :question/math-academy-id "q-335999" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=4).$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{7}{10}$ | $\\frac{9}{10}$ | $1$ |\n\n$P(X=4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,2,3})+P(X=4) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(X=4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4) & =F(4)-F(3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335999/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2bc3af7-207d-5f4f-9d8c-94f441ef1686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335991/field-1/e2eaf2af8b5790634cdea48914faf4267b26feb3802b9a1168212b81f436a7c0" :answer/id #uuid "8cbfda5b-e0b2-536d-9e88-d6fa5f369bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335991/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1d204c1-aa2c-5593-ab8f-983656d9778f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335991/field-1/e2eaf2af8b5790634cdea48914faf4267b26feb3802b9a1168212b81f436a7c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-335991/field-1/e2eaf2af8b5790634cdea48914faf4267b26feb3802b9a1168212b81f436a7c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335991" :question/id #uuid "d145f31d-0591-5990-a9cd-29377ad71a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335991" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.10$ | $0.40$ | $0.70$ | $1.00$ |\n\n$P(X=2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,1})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.70-0.40 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335991/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2bc3af7-207d-5f4f-9d8c-94f441ef1686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335991"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335992/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "4bd725b2-61c7-5164-aaf0-99f6805f4936" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335992/field-1/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe" :answer/id #uuid "8ad449da-5f5c-51ff-9c81-23900db287fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335992/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ad03197-562b-55f7-ac5a-5d59effa2486" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335992/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer-field/choices ["q-335992/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-335992/field-1/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335992" :question/id #uuid "fb7d294d-a75c-5b73-8d2c-100134dc6941" :question/math-academy-id "q-335992" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $0.60$ | $0.85$ | $1.00$ |\n\n$P(X=2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {-1,0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=-1)+P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {-1,0,1})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.60-0.35 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335992/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2bc3af7-207d-5f4f-9d8c-94f441ef1686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335992"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335993/field-1/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7" :answer/id #uuid "88f43d56-19a4-567d-b02b-f68e876fa26d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335993/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "26f24e4f-5965-5ad2-9a08-c92182017d2b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335993/field-1/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-335993/field-1/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335993" :question/id #uuid "ce49cb68-3db4-5f2e-b2ff-6a67857bace3" :question/math-academy-id "q-335993" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=5).$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.20$ | $0.45$ | $0.70$ | $0.90$ | $1.00$ |\n\n$P(X=5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {2,3,4,5}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {2,3,4})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.90-0.70 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335993/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2bc3af7-207d-5f4f-9d8c-94f441ef1686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335993"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83623"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<Y\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $a\\le Y\\le b,$ not $a<Y\\le b.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}$ to the form $a<Y\\le b.$ Looking at the given possible values of $Y,$ we see that $\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y$ is equivalent to $0<Y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}) & =P(0<Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =F(\\frac{3}{2})-F(0) \\\\  & =0.8-0.1 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "c4bc1443-6898-5da3-bfc3-69791c542ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "d041c975-2fcd-5824-98a8-6ec86e141af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "f19fcee4-41d0-5b27-bac5-597e4a0ee29b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "d7f7cf87-3f81-5498-a2a7-9a759a9ce3f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer/id #uuid "e8abe744-ca5b-5939-bc85-330a42777518" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6fafb2-5098-5a28-af87-16e659d7faec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83912/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer-field/choices ["q-83912/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-83912/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" "q-83912/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-83912/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" "q-83912/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83912" :question/id #uuid "2391c66e-53ee-59e5-b582-10c1ebef05d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-83912" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}).$\n\n| $y$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<Y\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $a<Y<b,$ not $a<Y\\le b.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}$ to the form $a<Y\\le b.$ Looking at the given possible values of $Y,$ we see that $Y<\\frac{5}{2}$ is equivalent to $Y\\le 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}) & =P(1<Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.7-0.3 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83912/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5f0085-01ab-5d16-884e-49200bc7ac14"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336006/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "30d218d8-e86a-5856-a7d1-261ba3d8c9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336006/field-1/8a0b0e90fe5f1e214b07031346ba3c8acbeca37470839c88e1ad9cdc97d00c5f" :answer/id #uuid "a0d61a3c-4cca-5d61-8b78-03114f119b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336006/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "22c2f73c-5f3f-5917-974c-4d152418c2c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336006/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-336006/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-336006/field-1/8a0b0e90fe5f1e214b07031346ba3c8acbeca37470839c88e1ad9cdc97d00c5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336006" :question/id #uuid "f31675fb-7b9f-56ca-bb9f-11863ce5b96e" :question/math-academy-id "q-336006" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(1<X\\le 3).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ | $\\frac{11}{20}$ | $\\frac{17}{20}$ | $1$ |\n\n$P(1<X\\le 3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 3) & =F(3)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{20}-\\frac{7}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336006/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5f0085-01ab-5d16-884e-49200bc7ac14"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336006"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83622"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(4<X\\le 6).$\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.9-0.4 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-124948/selection/f2288f9352f7ca2a51938247a89477aea196296ae7b20690ce35ebb30dfe5331" :answer/id #uuid "cdd60bfd-0742-5543-84a6-2ddcf32d16e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124948/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23