-- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ | $\\frac{13}{16}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.5<X\\le 0.5) & =F(0.5)-F(-1.5) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124948/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b5f0085-01ab-5d16-884e-49200bc7ac14"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124948"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "aba2036e-e47a-5aaa-aa54-0db64445e0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "3e332248-9058-56b2-a58d-573892499906" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer/id #uuid "f9b6e3be-37a6-50c0-b447-a824b5e3ff02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "11985619-0a2f-5b36-8eb7-fe875d8a7085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "cfd2d532-2f07-520f-ac29-6939255289a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "94300117-b42b-5d10-aeca-962af15cc7a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125069/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer-field/choices ["q-125069/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-125069/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" "q-125069/selection/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" "q-125069/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-125069/selection/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125069" :question/id #uuid "a4804377-f1ce-5af2-87e3-9a5ab39a2c13" :question/math-academy-id "q-125069" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X\\ge 6).$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(X\\ge 6).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $X\\ge 6,$ not $X>6.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $X\\ge 6$ to the form $X>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $X,$ we see that $X\\ge 6$ is equivalent to $X>4.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-125069/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "566f4fc1-ba4d-5433-9812-a3f5470e3d1e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "a340194f-670b-54f1-b058-7f93c268502f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "3aa8eed4-4378-502c-86a8-e07918ee8d89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" :answer/id #uuid "5c73188b-ba81-5125-87b6-334588dc02b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "c647e1bd-ef74-56a3-9bbb-023a9cafdffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer/id #uuid "b2dc37c3-d570-54a7-aa81-49a2c603f125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "526b7c9c-ad38-5c0b-a1be-ff73c1bf91af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124953/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer-field/choices ["q-124953/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-124953/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-124953/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" "q-124953/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-124953/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124953" :question/id #uuid "4e7c158a-ffa2-5597-bfaf-fa536f32bacf" :question/math-academy-id "q-124953" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X\\ge 5.5).$\n\n| $x$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ | $3.5$ | $4.5$ | $5.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(X\\ge 5.5).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $X\\ge 5.5,$ not $X>5.5.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $X\\ge 5.5$ to the form $X>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $X,$ we see that $X\\ge 5.5$ is equivalent to $X>4.5.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5.5) & =P(X>4.5) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4.5) \\\\  & =1-F(4.5) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124953/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "566f4fc1-ba4d-5433-9812-a3f5470e3d1e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124953"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83803"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X>4).$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "0aacac75-f6af-5286-a656-90f5f49ce9d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "87bcb633-4c69-5206-a876-f8941fff8dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "0124a23f-b0c8-5587-a119-a3d2457b3862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" :answer/id #uuid "54bda68d-eb95-5e03-9d3c-2c02f26d3875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "e39341f2-c55b-5590-805f-d553a4ed15df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9923ea10-554d-5568-a672-c7738c9ec4f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83921/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" :answer-field/choices ["q-83921/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-83921/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-83921/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-83921/selection/a272cbe64fea514fe5c8c9685aef2c9378fdfe44c54941c8bcba64a5f713bc84" "q-83921/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83921" :question/id #uuid "c28acbc7-f2e7-565f-8075-db60fccd70f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-83921" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $T$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(t)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(T\\ge 6).$\n\n| $t$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(t)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $T$ is a function $F(t)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(t)=P(T\\le t).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(T>a)=1-P(T\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(T\\ge 6).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $T\\ge 6,$ not $T>6.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $T\\ge 6$ to the form $T>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $T,$ we see that $T\\ge 6$ is equivalent to $T>3.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T\\ge 6) & =P(T>3) \\\\  & =1-P(T\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83921/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "566f4fc1-ba4d-5433-9812-a3f5470e3d1e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83921"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "e869b2e3-19bf-5a25-b7ca-1b78ec4ade84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "351f2887-7fd2-51f6-ad2c-625bce8dc7ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "7786a77e-fe1d-5c43-90b8-1cb0076d7da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "674c246f-bc68-5a37-9260-8688338873ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "005c06f9-ec19-5860-8d31-53b9d2d1f2ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1ff3b45-ef9b-534b-ae30-23a020e57474" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83922/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-83922/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-83922/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-83922/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-83922/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-83922/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83922" :question/id #uuid "b62816bd-c4e4-5f52-b9c3-0d50bd42682f" :question/math-academy-id "q-83922" :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $T$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(t)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(T\\ge 2).$\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(t)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{6}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $T$ is a function $F(t)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(t)=P(T\\le t).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(T>a)=1-P(T\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(T\\ge 2).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $T\\ge 2,$ not $T>2.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $T\\ge 2$ to the form $T>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $T,$ we see that $T\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $T>\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T\\ge 2) & =P(T>\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =1-P(T\\le \\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =1-F(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83922/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "566f4fc1-ba4d-5433-9812-a3f5470e3d1e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83922"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7379"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y),$ shown in the table below, and the cumulative distribution function $F(y),$ compute $F(2).$\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7382"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=5).$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ | $0.50$ | $0.90$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,3,5}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=3)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,3})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.50-0.45 \\\\  & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7381"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq  Y <     5 \\right).$\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a <            X \\leq b) = F(b) - F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq  Y <     5 \\right).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $a \\leq  Y <    b,$ not $a <           Y \\leq b.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $2 \\leq  Y <     5$ to the form $a <         X \\leq b.$ Looking at the given possible values of $Y,$ we see that $2 \\leq Y$ is equivalent to $1 <        Y,$ and  $Y<   5$ is equivalent to $Y \\leq 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le Y<5) & =P(1<Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7414"] :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X \\gt 2).$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.8$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-0.6 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
